  "worked_solution": "Let $p$ represent the profit on a single toss in the game. On each toss in the game, there are two possible outcomes:\n\n- If the coin lands on heads, the player wins $$5,$ so we have $p=5.$\n\n- If the coin lands on tails, the player loses $$4,$ so we have $p=-4.$\n\nLet's summarize this in a table.  If $p$ is the profit (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(p)$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{7}{10}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $p$ | $5$ | $-4$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[p] & =5\\cdot f(5)+(-4)\\cdot f(-4) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{3}{10})+(-4)(\\frac{7}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{10}-\\frac{28}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{15-28}{10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{10} \\\\  & =-1.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit is $-$\\,1.30.$",
